findings.description:
Nothing in the repo tests that M0's signal chain is synth -> filter -> destination. Proof by mutation: in a scratchpad copy of the repo I replaced the two lines in /workspaces/fableton/src/demo/engine.ts

    synth.output.connect(filter.input);
    filter.output.connect(destination);

with `synth.output.connect(destination);` (core.filter mounted but dangling, out of the audio path). Result: `npx vitest run` → 32 files / 359 tests passed, and `npx playwright test` against a production `--mode e2e` build of the mutated source → all 12 e2e tests passed, including e2e/audio/offline-render.spec.ts, which is the SS15 buffer proof and is even titled "…through synth -> filter -> destination". The unit test that claims to cover this (src/demo/engine.test.ts:99 "mounts the registered core devices and wires synth -> filter -> destination") asserts only (a) one worklet module was added, (b) exactly one FakeBiquadNode was created, (c) `anyNodeConnectsTo(base, base.destination)` — i.e. that *something* reaches the destination. It never asserts synth.output -> filter.input, nor filter.output -> destination, even though FakeAudioNode records every connection and `connectedNodeTypes()` already exists in src/devices/harness/testing/fakeAudio.ts for exactly this. So the load-bearing assembly step of M0 (the one piece of wiring the per-device tests cannot cover, since filter.test.ts/polySynth.test.ts only check each device's internal graph) has zero coverage in either the headless suite or the browser suite. Report only — I did not modify the repo.
